Camoufox: build the macOS bundle when the branding has no Assets.car.

Assets.car is compiled with actool, which only ships with Xcode on macOS;
elsewhere scripts/generate-assets-car.sh can only reuse an existing catalog.
Firefox used to copy it in browser/app/Makefile.in's repackage recipe, which
this patch made conditional. From Firefox 156 the bundle is declared with
MacOSBundle() in browser/app/moz.build and every extra file becomes a make
prerequisite of the bundle, so the same tolerance now lives where those
prerequisites are generated. Only that one file is optional.

diff --git a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py
index 33e69209c3..0174787548 100644
--- a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py
+++ b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py
@@ -1989,6 +1989,13 @@ class RecursiveMakeBackend(MakeBackend):
         for key in ("binaries", "extra_files"):
             for source, dest in spec[key]:
                 path = Path(context, source)
+                # Camoufox: the Assets.car icon catalog can only be compiled on
+                # macOS, so a branding built elsewhere may not have one. Bundle
+                # without it rather than failing on a missing prerequisite.
+                if dest == "Resources/Assets.car" and not os.path.exists(
+                    path.full_path
+                ):
+                    continue
                 resolved[key].append([path.full_path, dest])
                 inputs.append(path)
         if spec["stage"]:
